{"repositoryId":197448630,"availability":"available","full":"whiskyechobravo/kerkoapp","name":"kerkoapp","description":"A web application that provides a faceted search interface for bibliographies managed with Zotero.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":80,"forks":25,"created":"2019-07-17T19:17:27Z","updated":"2026-02-27T05:52:09Z","license":"BSD-3-Clause","branch":"main","homepage":"https://whiskyechobravo.github.io/kerko/","topics":["academia","bibliographies","bibliography","faceted-search","flask","flask-application","python","scholar","search-interface","webapp","zotero"],"demo":"https://demo.kerko.whiskyechobravo.com/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T19:32:52.971Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T19:32:52.971Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T19:32:52.971Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T19:32:52.971Z","stars":80,"forks":25}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["[KerkoApp] is a web application that uses [Kerko] to provide a user-friendly search and browsing interface for sharing a bibliography managed with the [Zotero] reference manager.","KerkoApp is built in [Python] with the [Flask] framework. It is just a thin container around Kerko and, as such, inherits most of its features directly from Kerko. However, it adds support for [TOML] configuration files, allowing a good separation of configuration from code.","Although KerkoApp offers many configuration options, more advanced customizations might require building a custom application, possibly using KerkoApp as a starting point, where various aspects of Kerko could be extended or adapted through its Python API."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/whiskyechobravo/kerkoapp/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"bbad32a92ecac9a44bbc071bff91dd602f758429977663a395947378592bed19","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T19:32:53.162Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T19:32:53.162Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"[KerkoAp